WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:04.558
(mellow smooth jazz music)

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:32.108
- Hello, I'm Bob Ross
and I'd like to welcome

00:00:32.108 --> 00:00:35.306
you to the 29th Joy of Painting series.

00:00:35.306 --> 00:00:36.766
If this is your first time with us,

00:00:36.766 --> 00:00:38.506
allow me to extend a personal invitation

00:00:38.506 --> 00:00:40.526
for you to get your
brushes and your paints

00:00:40.526 --> 00:00:42.406
and paint along with us each show.

00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:43.846
And if you've been with us before,

00:00:43.846 --> 00:00:45.665
please allow me to thank
you for inviting us

00:00:45.665 --> 00:00:48.145
back for another series of painting shows.

00:00:48.145 --> 00:00:49.524
We'll use about a dozen colors,

00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:52.401
some unorthodox brushes, and each show

00:00:52.401 --> 00:00:53.981
I'll show you how to put some of nature's

00:00:53.981 --> 00:00:56.341
masterpieces right here on the canvas.

00:00:56.341 --> 00:00:57.821
So, I'll tell you what, let's get started.

00:00:57.821 --> 00:00:58.900
Today, we'll have 'em run all the colors

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.000
across the screen, right there,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.219
that you need to paint along with us.

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:03.378
While they're doing that, let me tell you

00:01:03.378 --> 00:01:05.938
what I've got going on up here.

00:01:05.938 --> 00:01:08.738
Today, I'm using an 18 by 24 inch,

00:01:08.738 --> 00:01:10.598
double-primed, pre-stretched canvas,

00:01:10.598 --> 00:01:12.638
but you use whatever size you'd like.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.478
And I've just covered the entire canvas

00:01:14.478 --> 00:01:17.278
with a very thin coat of liquid white.

00:01:17.278 --> 00:01:18.698
Liquid white is designed just to make

00:01:18.698 --> 00:01:21.398
the canvas wet, and to make it slick.

00:01:21.398 --> 00:01:22.976
It allows us to actually blend color

00:01:22.976 --> 00:01:24.455
right here on the canvas.

00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:26.073
Makes your whole painting
life a lot easier.

00:01:26.073 --> 00:01:27.692
So, let's get started.

00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:29.212
Thought today we'd just do a very simple

00:01:29.212 --> 00:01:31.572
little scene that hope you'll enjoy.

00:01:31.572 --> 00:01:33.611
Let's start with a little two inch brush

00:01:33.611 --> 00:01:36.251
and a touch of the alizarin crimson.

00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:38.611
And we just load a little
bit right into the bristles.

00:01:38.611 --> 00:01:42.011
Pull a little paint out,
tap the bristles firmly

00:01:42.011 --> 00:01:44.089
to assure nice even distribution of paint

00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:45.648
all the way through the bristles.

00:01:45.648 --> 00:01:47.708
And let's go right up here.

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.166
And we'll take this old brush and just

00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:52.525
making little X's, little
criss-cross strokes.

00:01:52.525 --> 00:01:54.622
We'll just very quickly
drop in just a little

00:01:54.622 --> 00:01:57.222
warm part in the sky, here.

00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:59.182
Maybe we'll have a little pink in the sky.

00:01:59.182 --> 00:02:01.222
I sorta like that.

00:02:01.222 --> 00:02:03.602
And in our world, we can do anything

00:02:03.602 --> 00:02:07.442
that we want to do here, any old thing.

00:02:07.442 --> 00:02:09.179
There. Doesn't take too long when you're

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:12.198
using a brush that's two inches wide.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.635
Okay, without even cleaning the brush,

00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:18.374
we'll go right into, right
into a little phthalo blue.

00:02:18.374 --> 00:02:19.612
(chuckles) I like phthalo blue.

00:02:19.612 --> 00:02:22.551
It's a very warm blue, very nice.

00:02:22.551 --> 00:02:24.291
Once again, just tap
a little color into it

00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:26.531
and let's go back up here and still

00:02:26.531 --> 00:02:29.611
using our little criss-cross strokes, X's.

00:02:29.611 --> 00:02:31.973
That's all they are, little X's.

00:02:31.973 --> 00:02:34.553
We'll just apply a little
bit of the phthalo blue.

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.893
Somethin' about like so.

00:02:36.893 --> 00:02:38.153
Then we'll come back after we clean

00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:40.632
the brush and blend that together.

00:02:40.632 --> 00:02:42.790
Now, the blue is many many times

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.770
stronger than this little pink area.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.670
It'll just eat it up, so be careful.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.227
Be careful, all go away.

00:02:51.227 --> 00:02:52.326
If you wanted to make the indication

00:02:52.326 --> 00:02:55.196
of a happy little cloud, all
you do is just sorta tap.

00:02:55.196 --> 00:02:56.804
Little stringy cloud
just lives right there

00:02:56.804 --> 00:02:59.164
in the brush and that easy.

00:02:59.164 --> 00:03:03.204
We'll blend him out, have a
little stringer cloud there.

00:03:03.204 --> 00:03:04.802
Let's see, while we have that on there,

00:03:04.802 --> 00:03:06.159
let's have some water in this painting.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:10.559
I love water and it's very
easy to paint in this style.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:13.799
Still water is always level.

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:15.177
And I think today we'll have still water.

00:03:15.177 --> 00:03:19.597
So, pull from the outside in, outside in.

00:03:19.597 --> 00:03:24.237
Somethin' about like so. Alright.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.994
While I have that old brush going,

00:03:25.994 --> 00:03:28.174
I wanna darken the corners a little bit.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.569
I'ma take a little Prussian blue

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:32.008
and just add in the
corners here and there.

00:03:32.008 --> 00:03:34.287
Little bit up there, and we'll go over

00:03:34.287 --> 00:03:37.907
to the other side and add a little more

00:03:37.907 --> 00:03:40.827
and then down toward the bottom,

00:03:40.827 --> 00:03:42.345
and we'll put a little down here too.

00:03:42.345 --> 00:03:43.904
I'm just putting a little Prussian blue

00:03:43.904 --> 00:03:47.141
in each corner to darken it.

00:03:47.141 --> 00:03:48.877
And then, the most fun part of this

00:03:48.877 --> 00:03:52.316
whole technique is washing the brushes.

00:03:52.316 --> 00:03:54.976
Since these are oil paints, we're washing

00:03:54.976 --> 00:03:57.615
our brushes with odorless paint thinner.

00:03:57.615 --> 00:04:00.194
Shake off the excess,
(paint brush thumps)

00:04:00.194 --> 00:04:02.693
(giggles) and just beat
the devil out of it.

00:04:02.693 --> 00:04:04.969
That's really the most fun part of it.

00:04:04.969 --> 00:04:07.529
Now, with a clean brush,
and it's relatively

00:04:07.529 --> 00:04:09.969
dry from just beating it, we'll start

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:12.329
in the light area, which is the pink,

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:14.727
and we'll blend it all together.

00:04:14.727 --> 00:04:19.265
Somethin' about like so.
That's all there is to it.

00:04:19.265 --> 00:04:23.162
Okay, and down here, we'll
just do the same thing.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:27.502
There. But it's that easy, that easy.

00:04:27.502 --> 00:04:31.142
What's so fantastic about
this is that anybody,

00:04:31.142 --> 00:04:34.782
anybody can put a little
masterpiece on canvas

00:04:34.782 --> 00:04:36.942
with just a little bit of practice,

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:40.142
a vision in your mind, and off you go.

00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:42.261
Alright, that's working so well.

00:04:42.261 --> 00:04:46.440
Take a little white,
little bit of the blue,

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.979
grab a little more of the titanium white.

00:04:47.979 --> 00:04:49.553
I wanna make a light blue color here,

00:04:49.553 --> 00:04:52.273
mostly phthalo blue, and let's just

00:04:52.273 --> 00:04:54.833
tap a little color into the bristles.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:56.733
This old two inch brush'll
do marvelous things.

00:04:56.733 --> 00:04:58.852
Watch here, watch here, watch here.

00:04:58.852 --> 00:05:02.052
It's fun. Take the corner of the brush

00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:06.091
and just pull down,
somethin' about like so.

00:05:06.091 --> 00:05:07.451
Straight down, straight down.

00:05:07.451 --> 00:05:09.671
I wanna make it look
like little distant trees

00:05:09.671 --> 00:05:12.571
live far back in the distance.

00:05:12.571 --> 00:05:15.211
Little more color, and we'll just have it,

00:05:15.211 --> 00:05:18.111
we'll go, I don't know, right there.

00:05:18.111 --> 00:05:22.491
In your world, you create
any illusion that you want.

00:05:22.491 --> 00:05:24.229
There, but I wanna keep the bottom light,

00:05:24.229 --> 00:05:25.649
so it looks like mist.

00:05:25.649 --> 00:05:27.689
You could even take another two inch

00:05:27.689 --> 00:05:32.295
brush, I have several, and tap it.

00:05:32.295 --> 00:05:35.565
Really get in there and tap
it and then lift upward.

00:05:35.565 --> 00:05:37.903
It'll help create that illusion of mist,

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:40.442
right down at the bottom.

00:05:40.442 --> 00:05:42.662
And sometimes, sometimes it's a lot

00:05:42.662 --> 00:05:45.041
of fun to put several layers.

00:05:45.041 --> 00:05:47.501
It helps create depth in your painting

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.641
and for that, we'll add a little more blue

00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:51.334
but we make it a little darker.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:53.294
Add a little Prussian blue to it,

00:05:53.294 --> 00:05:56.034
make it a little darker,
but the same thing.

00:05:56.034 --> 00:05:58.094
And we'll come back and just put

00:05:58.094 --> 00:06:00.593
another little layer
in here, just touching

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:04.011
and pulling downward,
that's all we're doing.

00:06:04.011 --> 00:06:05.951
That's really all we're doing.

00:06:05.951 --> 00:06:10.251
Somethin' about like that. There.

00:06:10.251 --> 00:06:11.509
And we don't know where that goes.

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:13.669
It doesn't matter at this point.

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:16.829
And back to our other two inch
brush, and we'll tap this.

00:06:16.829 --> 00:06:20.759
I wanna create mist again.
Notice the separation.

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:23.308
It's caused because of
the difference in color,

00:06:23.308 --> 00:06:26.688
difference in value, and that misty area

00:06:26.688 --> 00:06:29.088
turns out to be your very best friend.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:32.928
Take care of it, treasure it. There.

00:06:32.928 --> 00:06:36.348
Okay, let's have some more fun. (chuckles)

00:06:36.348 --> 00:06:38.667
Let's see, gonna take some black,

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:42.566
some Prussian blue, and
a little phthalo blue.

00:06:42.566 --> 00:06:43.964
It doesn't matter, we'll
just throw it on there.

00:06:43.964 --> 00:06:48.563
Crimson too, what the
heck. Be brave, be brave.

00:06:48.563 --> 00:06:50.180
I'm gonna put a little
satin green in there too.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.460
It's getting close enough we should begin

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:55.140
seeing some color. Little bit of white.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.460
Don't want it totally dark yet.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:02.758
There, perfect. 'Kay I'm
gonna wipe the old knife off.

00:07:02.758 --> 00:07:07.495
And let's get us fan brush,
we'll use a fan brush.

00:07:07.495 --> 00:07:11.135
Load it full of color,
both sides, both sides.

00:07:11.135 --> 00:07:14.275
'Kay, let's go up in here
and maybe in our world

00:07:14.275 --> 00:07:18.715
there lives, does now, some
little trees back in here.

00:07:18.715 --> 00:07:20.311
Now, these are a little
closer, you're seeing

00:07:20.311 --> 00:07:25.211
a little more detail, a
little more distinct. There.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.411
And we just drop 'em in.

00:07:27.411 --> 00:07:31.065
We don't know where they
go, wherever you want 'em.

00:07:31.065 --> 00:07:34.745
That's exactly, exactly
where they should live.

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:36.645
Don't put too much detail in here.

00:07:36.645 --> 00:07:39.925
It's too far away, you're not
gonna see a lot of detail.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:42.465
You see detail when
it's very close to you.

00:07:42.465 --> 00:07:43.804
When things are far away, you make out

00:07:43.804 --> 00:07:47.363
form, shape, basic color, that's all.

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.942
Save the detail till the foreground.

00:07:51.942 --> 00:07:54.580
The lack of detail helps also create

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:58.340
that illusion of distance
and depth in your painting.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:01.780
It's very very important, very important.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:05.320
M'kay, I'm gonna tap a little of that.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.780
That'll help create that
illusion of mist on there too.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:12.440
There. Lift slightly upward, lightly.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.180
Just a little bit, see? Now then.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.497
You know, when I was a traditional painter

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.236
one of the hardest things to make

00:08:19.236 --> 00:08:21.372
effectively was reflections.

00:08:21.372 --> 00:08:24.530
Watch how easy, I'll take
some of that same color,

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:28.430
we'll take a two inch
brush, touch and pull down.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:29.829
Just pull straight down.

00:08:29.829 --> 00:08:33.909
It's most important that
we go straight down.

00:08:33.909 --> 00:08:36.866
Somethin' like so, straight down.

00:08:36.866 --> 00:08:39.726
(clicks tongue) make those little noises.

00:08:39.726 --> 00:08:43.565
Then, very lightly, go across. There.

00:08:43.565 --> 00:08:48.385
And instantly, we have some
nice reflections, that simple.

00:08:48.385 --> 00:08:49.284
Now, here somethin' is funny.

00:08:49.284 --> 00:08:51.824
Take a little, I just use a little white.

00:08:51.824 --> 00:08:53.863
If you wanna create another
plane in your painting,

00:08:53.863 --> 00:08:56.643
take a little white and lift upward,

00:08:56.643 --> 00:08:57.981
and it'll make little areas back here

00:08:57.981 --> 00:09:00.160
that looks like a whole different plane

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.416
and the white will look like
little trunks in those trees.

00:09:04.416 --> 00:09:06.775
There, that easy.

00:09:06.775 --> 00:09:07.834
Let's put a little water line.

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:10.453
For that we use liquid white.

00:09:10.453 --> 00:09:12.853
Pull it out very flat,
flat as you can get it,

00:09:12.853 --> 00:09:15.213
cut across, 'kay?

00:09:15.213 --> 00:09:18.348
And we can go right up in here

00:09:18.348 --> 00:09:21.727
and we can just drop in
just a little water line.

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.627
Just a happy little water line lives back

00:09:23.627 --> 00:09:26.986
in here somewhere, we
don't know where it is.

00:09:26.986 --> 00:09:28.506
Don't know that we even
care, just let your

00:09:28.506 --> 00:09:30.926
imagination take you
anywhere you wanna go.

00:09:30.926 --> 00:09:33.546
Lotta times I start a
painting and have nothing

00:09:33.546 --> 00:09:38.505
in mind but the time of
day and the time of year.

00:09:38.505 --> 00:09:42.943
And from that, you can paint
some fantastic little scenes.

00:09:42.943 --> 00:09:44.302
Don't worry about it, you don't always

00:09:44.302 --> 00:09:46.562
have to have a perfect vision in your mind

00:09:46.562 --> 00:09:48.918
of what it is you're gonna paint.

00:09:48.918 --> 00:09:52.938
Imagination is, it's like any
other muscle in your body,

00:09:52.938 --> 00:09:54.729
or lack of muscle in your body.

00:09:54.729 --> 00:09:58.069
The more you practice,
the better it becomes.

00:09:58.069 --> 00:10:00.308
Take some black, Prussian blue,

00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:02.446
I'ma put some phthalo green in there.

00:10:02.446 --> 00:10:06.346
I like phthalo green,
maybe a little crimson.

00:10:06.346 --> 00:10:08.906
There we go.

00:10:08.906 --> 00:10:11.706
Alright, let me wipe off the knife.

00:10:11.706 --> 00:10:15.585
I just wipe the knife on a
little, little paper towel.

00:10:15.585 --> 00:10:18.805
I would just use that
brush, little fan brush.

00:10:18.805 --> 00:10:22.163
Load some color into it,
both sides of the brush.

00:10:22.163 --> 00:10:24.443
Both side, let's go up in here.

00:10:24.443 --> 00:10:28.103
Let's have, let's have
a little evergreen tree.

00:10:28.103 --> 00:10:29.910
He lives right here, see?

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.270
Just make a line, take the corner

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:34.310
of your brush, make a
touch, make another one,

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:37.150
and just sort of work from the center out.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.010
There it goes. (clicks tongue)

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.907
It's easier to do 'em fast
than it is slow, though.

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:43.905
Here they come. (clicks tongue)

00:10:43.905 --> 00:10:45.485
Just sorta back and forth.

00:10:45.485 --> 00:10:47.495
I had a lady in class one time tell me

00:10:47.495 --> 00:10:50.978
it was like makin' Z's, the letter Z.

00:10:50.978 --> 00:10:54.438
She called 'em Z trees, so I guess

00:10:54.438 --> 00:10:56.957
that's as good of analogy as any.

00:10:56.957 --> 00:10:58.357
From the center out,
the center of the tree

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:02.116
should be the thickest, darkest,
strongest part of the tree

00:11:02.116 --> 00:11:03.395
'cause you have leaves on the back,

00:11:03.395 --> 00:11:05.315
you have a trunk in the middle,

00:11:05.315 --> 00:11:06.995
and you have leaves on this side.

00:11:06.995 --> 00:11:10.375
We'll have one more in there. There we go.

00:11:10.375 --> 00:11:12.975
Have a little family of trees.

00:11:12.975 --> 00:11:15.955
You know if you've painted with me before,

00:11:15.955 --> 00:11:18.795
I think everybody should
have a friend, even a tree.

00:11:18.795 --> 00:11:21.375
Even a tree needs a friend.

00:11:21.375 --> 00:11:22.814
Now, if you wanted to reflect those,

00:11:22.814 --> 00:11:25.232
just pop in some general indications

00:11:25.232 --> 00:11:27.696
of where they are, no big deal.

00:11:29.568 --> 00:11:31.285
'Cause we don't make mistakes here,

00:11:31.285 --> 00:11:33.804
we have happy accidents.

00:11:33.804 --> 00:11:37.464
Very quickly, you learn to work
with anything that happens.

00:11:37.464 --> 00:11:39.839
Take the big brush, pull
down. (clicks tongue)

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:42.579
Straight down, once
again, and then go across,

00:11:42.579 --> 00:11:46.599
and we have instant reflections.

00:11:46.599 --> 00:11:47.817
I'ma just use that same fan brush.

00:11:47.817 --> 00:11:49.617
It has that color we
made the tree out of it

00:11:49.617 --> 00:11:53.116
and I'll go through cad yellow
and a little yellow ochre.

00:11:53.116 --> 00:11:55.726
Immediately, we have green.

00:11:55.726 --> 00:11:57.934
There we are. Let's go up in here.

00:11:57.934 --> 00:12:00.951
And we can take that green, let's go back

00:12:00.951 --> 00:12:02.067
and put some highlights on our little

00:12:02.067 --> 00:12:05.846
evergreen trees, there
they go. (clicks tongue)

00:12:05.846 --> 00:12:09.186
Alright, this little tree here he's sayin,

00:12:09.186 --> 00:12:12.146
"Don't leave me out. I need some too."

00:12:12.146 --> 00:12:14.846
There we are, there we are, there we are.

00:12:14.846 --> 00:12:17.206
Alright, now, gonna put
a little liquid white

00:12:17.206 --> 00:12:19.046
right on that same brush, 'cause I wanna

00:12:19.046 --> 00:12:22.005
lighten the color and
make it a little thinner.

00:12:22.005 --> 00:12:24.745
A thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:12:24.745 --> 00:12:28.065
We mix 'em back up again,
just go back up here.

00:12:28.065 --> 00:12:29.505
And we can just take this brush

00:12:29.505 --> 00:12:32.545
and let's just pop in the indication

00:12:32.545 --> 00:12:34.945
of some little bushes that live down here,

00:12:34.945 --> 00:12:37.585
right down in these little foots.

00:12:37.585 --> 00:12:40.621
Somethin' about like that. How's that?

00:12:40.621 --> 00:12:41.640
That looks like a little island.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.739
Let's put some dirt there.

00:12:43.739 --> 00:12:47.299
Let's take some white, little dark sienna,

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:49.879
mix 'em together, cut off
a little roll of paint.

00:12:49.879 --> 00:12:53.439
Let's go up in here and we'll take this

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:55.759
and we just put the indication here,

00:12:55.759 --> 00:12:58.519
a little bit of soil,
some dirt, some kind.

00:12:58.519 --> 00:12:59.475
Gotta have a little place, if this is

00:12:59.475 --> 00:13:02.879
a little island, for all this to sit on.

00:13:02.892 --> 00:13:06.084
Alright. See there?

00:13:06.084 --> 00:13:08.322
That's all there is to it.

00:13:08.322 --> 00:13:11.681
M'kay, (sucks teeth),
alright, we gotta figure out

00:13:11.681 --> 00:13:13.140
somethin' to do on the other side now.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:16.580
Let's have some fun, let's have some fun.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.980
You know if you've painted with me before,

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.060
I like old big trees.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.740
Let's take a little bit
of that color right there,

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.359
let's go right up in here.

00:13:25.359 --> 00:13:27.499
This is your bravery test, take the corner

00:13:27.499 --> 00:13:29.996
of the old two inch brush and let's just

00:13:29.996 --> 00:13:33.376
begin laying in a basic shape here.

00:13:33.376 --> 00:13:37.845
Tree it lives right there, right there.

00:13:37.845 --> 00:13:41.417
Big old tree, but he's a nice tree.

00:13:41.417 --> 00:13:43.777
There he is.

00:13:43.777 --> 00:13:46.216
Alright, while I got that brush going,

00:13:46.216 --> 00:13:49.156
I tell you what, maybe let's do somethin'

00:13:49.156 --> 00:13:52.376
about like this. (clicks tongue)

00:13:52.376 --> 00:13:55.512
And we just tap in all kinds of little,

00:13:55.512 --> 00:13:58.171
little bushy lookin' areas.

00:13:58.171 --> 00:14:00.551
You have to decide what lives here,

00:14:00.551 --> 00:14:03.041
how far it goes, how tall
is it, how short is it,

00:14:03.041 --> 00:14:08.001
it's fat, skinny, in
between, it's your world.

00:14:08.001 --> 00:14:11.819
And in your world, you
make all the decisions.

00:14:11.819 --> 00:14:14.947
All the decisions. There we are.

00:14:14.947 --> 00:14:16.507
See, we're just puttin' some dark in here

00:14:16.507 --> 00:14:20.575
so later on, our light color will show.

00:14:20.575 --> 00:14:21.801
We'll just grab a--
(paint brush clatters)

00:14:21.801 --> 00:14:23.839
Oops, grab another one.

00:14:23.839 --> 00:14:25.554
There's a fan brush right there.

00:14:25.554 --> 00:14:30.173
Take a little white, a little
bit of the dark sienna,

00:14:30.173 --> 00:14:31.652
just wanna make the indication here.

00:14:31.652 --> 00:14:34.489
Maybe a little tree trunk,
maybe a little more dark sienna.

00:14:34.489 --> 00:14:37.187
(exhales quickly) That's nice.

00:14:37.187 --> 00:14:40.667
'Kay, right here. (exhales)

00:14:40.667 --> 00:14:41.785
Just want some indications.

00:14:41.785 --> 00:14:43.264
I'ma put some happy
little leaves in there,

00:14:43.264 --> 00:14:46.723
so we're gonna cover most of those up.

00:14:46.723 --> 00:14:49.841
Most of 'em won't show,
we'll go right into that.

00:14:49.841 --> 00:14:54.160
Need a little sap green,
little bit of the yellow.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:54.799
We'll just put it right on this

00:14:54.799 --> 00:14:57.399
two inch brush, give a little push.

00:14:57.399 --> 00:14:59.799
Good shot there, you can see that well.

00:14:59.799 --> 00:15:01.539
'Kay, let's go up in here.

00:15:01.539 --> 00:15:05.158
Now, I wanna put some leaves on here.

00:15:05.158 --> 00:15:07.218
Use just the corner of the brush,

00:15:07.218 --> 00:15:11.378
just the corner of the brush. There we go.

00:15:11.378 --> 00:15:15.257
See? That's all there is
to it, just the corner.

00:15:15.257 --> 00:15:18.077
Think about shape and form, drop these

00:15:18.077 --> 00:15:22.655
little rascals in wherever you want 'em.

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:24.895
Wherever. You really are the creator

00:15:24.895 --> 00:15:25.991
on this piece of canvas.

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:27.731
You can do anything!

00:15:27.731 --> 00:15:30.691
You can move rivers, mountains,

00:15:30.691 --> 00:15:32.910
create any illusion that you want here.

00:15:35.126 --> 00:15:37.686
When I go home, the only power
I have is over the garbage.

00:15:37.686 --> 00:15:40.046
I can take it to the street all by myself,

00:15:40.046 --> 00:15:44.746
but here I can do anything,
absolutely anything.

00:15:44.746 --> 00:15:48.102
I decided I wanted a bush right there.

00:15:48.102 --> 00:15:52.582
And, tell you what,

00:15:52.582 --> 00:15:53.734
let's get crazy.

00:15:53.734 --> 00:15:56.712
You know me, if you've
painted with me before.

00:15:56.712 --> 00:15:59.932
I like big trees and we have one

00:15:59.932 --> 00:16:04.012
living in our world right there.

00:16:04.012 --> 00:16:06.232
There he comes.

00:16:06.232 --> 00:16:07.752
We should've done this
with the two inch brush,

00:16:07.752 --> 00:16:11.970
it'd been a lot faster. There we go.

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:15.632
Just drop it in wherever
you think it should be.

00:16:17.688 --> 00:16:21.400
Alright. Boy, that's a big tree,

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:25.539
I wasn't kiddin', this is a monster tree.

00:16:25.539 --> 00:16:28.478
Huge tree and you could've done it

00:16:28.478 --> 00:16:32.658
with a two inch brush just
as easy, but much quicker.

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:36.757
I like the old fan brush, it
gives you a little more detail.

00:16:36.757 --> 00:16:39.696
Here we go with a smaller tree,

00:16:39.696 --> 00:16:42.844
'cause I think he needs a friend.

00:16:42.844 --> 00:16:47.289
There. 'Kay, just drop it in.

00:16:47.289 --> 00:16:48.908
All we're doing, once again, is putting

00:16:48.908 --> 00:16:50.948
in the background color.

00:16:50.948 --> 00:16:53.668
You could put this in with a paint roller,

00:16:53.668 --> 00:16:57.128
it doesn't matter, long
as the shape is right.

00:16:57.128 --> 00:16:58.548
We'll come back and separate all

00:16:58.548 --> 00:17:01.346
of this with some nice highlights.

00:17:01.346 --> 00:17:04.526
Here's a little brown and white.

00:17:04.526 --> 00:17:07.546
We're gonna put the
indication just here and there

00:17:07.546 --> 00:17:11.646
of a trunk, just what you
can see, here and there.

00:17:11.646 --> 00:17:13.205
There. You don't see
it all 'cause you have

00:17:13.205 --> 00:17:15.945
leaves on this side.

00:17:15.945 --> 00:17:18.083
We can go back to our little fan brush,

00:17:18.083 --> 00:17:21.473
go right through the cad
yellow, yellow ochre.

00:17:21.473 --> 00:17:23.342
We'll load some color into it.

00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:25.182
Let's go back up in here.

00:17:25.182 --> 00:17:28.761
Let's put a highlight or two on here.

00:17:28.761 --> 00:17:32.901
Evergreens are normally
darker than other trees,

00:17:32.901 --> 00:17:36.777
so don't kill all the dark
here in your evergreen.

00:17:36.777 --> 00:17:38.717
It happens sometime,
get's ya' feeling good

00:17:38.717 --> 00:17:41.197
and you don't know when to stop.

00:17:41.197 --> 00:17:44.537
There. And the base of the tree should be

00:17:44.537 --> 00:17:49.107
darker than the top, big
shadow areas underneath.

00:17:49.107 --> 00:17:53.814
And those shadow areas are where
all my little friends live.

00:17:53.814 --> 00:17:56.293
In previous shows we've had, like Peapod

00:17:56.293 --> 00:17:59.452
the pocket squirrel, my little
squirrel that lives with me.

00:17:59.452 --> 00:18:01.193
We've had him on the show.

00:18:01.193 --> 00:18:03.971
But this is kinda the
places that he likes.

00:18:03.971 --> 00:18:07.651
Let's take a little bit of color,

00:18:07.651 --> 00:18:10.510
let's use the, let's
use the one inch brush.

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.930
We'll go through some, get some sap green,

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:15.850
some yellow, load a lotta
color into the brush.

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:19.610
More sap green. (sharply
exhales) That's nice.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.669
Alright, then we can go up here,

00:18:21.669 --> 00:18:24.528
and we can begin picking
out individual bushes,

00:18:24.528 --> 00:18:27.267
one at a time, one at a time.

00:18:27.267 --> 00:18:29.987
There's a happy little
bush, lives right there.

00:18:29.987 --> 00:18:32.758
You knew he was there, didn't you?

00:18:32.758 --> 00:18:35.619
And he's got a little friend named Clyde,

00:18:35.619 --> 00:18:38.958
lives right over here, there he is.

00:18:38.958 --> 00:18:41.439
So you can give all these things names,

00:18:41.439 --> 00:18:44.899
personalities, it's okay.

00:18:44.899 --> 00:18:46.499
We'll take the little oval brush,

00:18:46.499 --> 00:18:48.877
dipped in some paint thinner.

00:18:48.877 --> 00:18:52.397
We'll go through some
midnight black and some brown

00:18:52.397 --> 00:18:57.397
on one, wanna load it full of color again.

00:18:57.643 --> 00:19:00.103
Then I'ma take, and with the other side,

00:19:00.103 --> 00:19:02.202
I got some light brown I made earlier.

00:19:02.202 --> 00:19:04.822
I'm just gonna go through, see?

00:19:04.822 --> 00:19:05.951
Like that, put a little black in it,

00:19:05.951 --> 00:19:08.000
make it a little dark, ooh that's nice.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.938
Now, with that I guess we'll come up here

00:19:10.938 --> 00:19:13.417
and make the indication, we can't see

00:19:13.417 --> 00:19:16.538
too much of 'em, of some
rocks that live up there.

00:19:18.552 --> 00:19:20.308
Just some happy little rocks.

00:19:20.308 --> 00:19:24.709
Maybe there's one
(exhales) there, somethin'.

00:19:24.709 --> 00:19:28.208
Wherever, just some indications.

00:19:28.208 --> 00:19:31.329
Then we'll come back with our brush

00:19:31.329 --> 00:19:33.768
we were making the bushes with

00:19:33.768 --> 00:19:37.689
and we'll settle those right
down into the painting.

00:19:37.689 --> 00:19:39.928
There, now see?

00:19:39.928 --> 00:19:42.969
Now they become part of the painting.

00:19:42.969 --> 00:19:46.609
There we go, just like so.

00:19:46.609 --> 00:19:49.069
And we'll make all kinds
of little bushes and trees

00:19:49.069 --> 00:19:51.749
and happy little things
that live here in our world.

00:19:53.902 --> 00:19:55.388
Alright.

00:19:57.578 --> 00:20:01.379
Okay. Shoot, if we had
such a place as that,

00:20:01.379 --> 00:20:03.119
I'd have to go fishin' there.

00:20:03.119 --> 00:20:06.135
I like to fish but I'm
not a very good fisherman.

00:20:06.135 --> 00:20:08.028
I catch a little fish and
take the hook carefully

00:20:08.028 --> 00:20:10.387
out of his mouth and
put a band-aid on him,

00:20:10.387 --> 00:20:12.547
little CPR, pat him on the toot toot,

00:20:12.547 --> 00:20:14.142
and put him back in the water,

00:20:14.142 --> 00:20:17.762
go back, catch him again another day.

00:20:17.762 --> 00:20:19.082
But we'd have to have a way to get up here

00:20:19.082 --> 00:20:20.222
if we're gonna catch that fish.

00:20:20.222 --> 00:20:22.841
We'll take a little of the van dyke brown

00:20:22.841 --> 00:20:26.182
and let's have us a little path.

00:20:26.182 --> 00:20:27.742
We had to walk all through
through these bushes,

00:20:27.742 --> 00:20:31.160
maskeeters would get us, so let's have us

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.858
a little path that we
can walk back in here,

00:20:34.858 --> 00:20:37.338
catch a big old trout or bass, whatever

00:20:37.338 --> 00:20:40.258
it is that lives in here. There.

00:20:40.258 --> 00:20:43.618
Take a little bit, let's find some white,

00:20:43.618 --> 00:20:46.597
little dark sienna, mix it together,

00:20:46.597 --> 00:20:48.458
make a little highlight color.

00:20:48.458 --> 00:20:50.438
Just barely touching, barely.

00:20:50.438 --> 00:20:52.509
Let it graze, let it graze.

00:20:52.509 --> 00:20:56.529
That easy, that easy.

00:20:56.529 --> 00:20:58.761
'Bout like so.

00:20:58.761 --> 00:21:02.220
M'kay. There.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:06.139
Now then, let's put
somethin' on this side.

00:21:06.139 --> 00:21:08.899
Ya have somethin' on
the other side the path,

00:21:08.899 --> 00:21:11.297
now let's go on this side.

00:21:11.297 --> 00:21:13.717
Once again, I'ma take a one inch brush

00:21:13.717 --> 00:21:14.893
and I'm just settin' it straight down

00:21:14.893 --> 00:21:16.593
and I'm pulling it in one direction.

00:21:16.593 --> 00:21:19.633
It's most, most important.

00:21:19.633 --> 00:21:22.633
That loads a lot of paint,
and see it rounds one edge.

00:21:22.633 --> 00:21:26.173
You wanna turn it, put that
rounded edge to the top.

00:21:26.173 --> 00:21:27.693
It's most important.

00:21:27.693 --> 00:21:30.813
Then we take that, we go right up in here,

00:21:30.813 --> 00:21:32.793
no pressure hardly, just enough to get

00:21:32.793 --> 00:21:35.353
the brush to touch the canvas,

00:21:35.353 --> 00:21:37.553
and we begin working on shape and form

00:21:37.553 --> 00:21:41.273
and we create a bush or
tree that lives right there.

00:21:41.273 --> 00:21:43.113
That's all there is to it.

00:21:43.113 --> 00:21:46.873
And there's another one,
but do one at a time.

00:21:46.873 --> 00:21:51.053
I know, I know. Sometimes it
starts working, you get greedy.

00:21:51.053 --> 00:21:54.113
Do one at a time, one at a time.

00:21:54.113 --> 00:21:56.173
I'ma put a little bright red on there.

00:21:56.173 --> 00:21:57.933
Maybe here's one right here. Oh, yeah.

00:21:57.933 --> 00:21:59.367
It's got little, I don't
know if you can see 'em,

00:21:59.367 --> 00:22:01.806
I got little red flowers on the tip.

00:22:01.806 --> 00:22:04.794
(chuckles) Sneaky. There.

00:22:06.544 --> 00:22:08.203
Then we can go back over in here,

00:22:08.203 --> 00:22:11.481
and we can begin adding in just little

00:22:11.481 --> 00:22:14.469
things that come about here on the path.

00:22:14.469 --> 00:22:19.437
'Bout like that. Alright, alright.

00:22:19.437 --> 00:22:21.072
You got your brushes warmed up yet

00:22:21.072 --> 00:22:24.050
and you're ready, you can do this!

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:26.570
You can do this, I know you can.

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:28.650
I get letters every day from people

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:31.850
all over the country
that said they'd never

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:34.610
believed they could paint
and they're doing it.

00:22:34.610 --> 00:22:36.190
Their friends and
neighbors don't believe it

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:40.510
when they look at their
paintings but they are doing it.

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:41.850
There. I'ma put a little stick

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:44.970
lives right there, little old tree.

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:48.347
Maybe, maybe, maybe this little tree died

00:22:48.347 --> 00:22:52.427
and he's naked now, just a
skeleton hangin' out here.

00:22:52.427 --> 00:22:54.767
And that happens in nature.

00:22:54.767 --> 00:22:56.767
There. So, we can put little arms on him

00:22:56.767 --> 00:23:00.470
that are still hangin' out. Alright.

00:23:02.719 --> 00:23:05.158
All kinds of little dooders.

00:23:05.158 --> 00:23:07.718
Maybe over in here, and
these little details

00:23:07.718 --> 00:23:10.636
are what'll make your painting
look a little more finished.

00:23:10.636 --> 00:23:12.156
Take your time when you're doing these

00:23:12.156 --> 00:23:16.615
and just drop 'em in here and
there and there and wherever.

00:23:16.615 --> 00:23:20.215
Take a little light brown
with paint thinner on it

00:23:20.215 --> 00:23:22.375
and when you mix this, get it very thin.

00:23:22.375 --> 00:23:26.875
This should be almost like,
almost ink consistency.

00:23:26.875 --> 00:23:29.835
Turn the bristles, that'll
bring it to a very sharp point.

00:23:29.835 --> 00:23:33.595
There you see it good
against that dark, alright?

00:23:33.595 --> 00:23:36.235
And where it's very dark, then
we make little light trees.

00:23:36.235 --> 00:23:38.613
Where it's light, we make dark trees

00:23:38.613 --> 00:23:41.143
because they both exist in nature.

00:23:41.143 --> 00:23:43.172
So you can put little, see now there's

00:23:43.172 --> 00:23:47.452
a little tree lives back
here, just has a good time,

00:23:47.452 --> 00:23:52.031
looks out over the
water, talks to the fish.

00:23:52.031 --> 00:23:54.211
That's all there is to it.

00:23:54.211 --> 00:23:55.731
Another way of making
little sticks and twigs,

00:23:55.731 --> 00:23:59.051
take your knife, just a clean knife

00:23:59.051 --> 00:24:00.986
and you can reach up in here and just

00:24:00.986 --> 00:24:03.866
scrape right through the paint, see?

00:24:03.866 --> 00:24:06.026
And that'll make all kinda little sticks.

00:24:06.026 --> 00:24:06.881
And let's come down here,

00:24:06.881 --> 00:24:10.141
we'll make a few more in here, wherever.

00:24:10.141 --> 00:24:12.261
You decide where they live.

00:24:12.261 --> 00:24:13.760
Sometimes, these old evergreens here

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.579
have old dead limbs hangin' off of 'em

00:24:16.579 --> 00:24:20.579
and you can do that, just with
a little flick of the knife.

00:24:20.579 --> 00:24:21.739
And shoot, with that I think we

00:24:21.739 --> 00:24:24.217
'bout have a finished painting.

00:24:24.217 --> 00:24:25.317
It's that easy.

00:24:25.317 --> 00:24:27.457
Let's take a little bit
of the paint thinner,

00:24:27.457 --> 00:24:31.503
little bright red, and we'll
sign this little rascal.

00:24:31.503 --> 00:24:33.672
Really hope you've enjoyed it.

00:24:33.672 --> 00:24:36.972
It's a very simple
painting that you can do

00:24:36.972 --> 00:24:38.372
and if you try it, I'd love to see

00:24:38.372 --> 00:24:39.750
some photographs of what you're doing.

00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:42.070
So if you have time, take a photograph,

00:24:42.070 --> 00:24:43.990
send it to us, let us hear from you.

00:24:43.990 --> 00:24:46.350
Until then, from all of us here,

00:24:46.350 --> 00:24:48.510
I'd like to wish you happy painting

00:24:48.510 --> 00:24:50.328
and God bless, my friend.

00:24:50.328 --> 00:24:53.542
(mellow smooth jazz music)

